{"seq":1,"at":"2026-09-17","kind":"imported","target":{"type":"article","id":"a1106"},"reason":"Article of the Quiztopia bank (written for card c093): researched and transcribed in September 2026, converted to the quiz platform on 2026-10-20.","by":"Quiztopia import","ref":"quiz-archive/transcripts/quiztopia/c093.json"},
{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a1106"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge literature/children-lit","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/literature__children-lit.g2.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",828],["+","The Belgian magazine „Spirou“ produced a sidekick wilder than any dog. On 31 January 1952 André Franquin let Spirou and Fantasio bring home a Marsupilami, a feisty black-and-yellow creature from the South American jungle of Palombia, spotted like a leopard and equipped with an absurdly long prehensile tail that it uses as fist, spring and lasso. It rarely says more than „Houba! Houba!“, yet it soon outgrew the series and got albums, cartoons and films of its own.\n\n"],["=",87],["+","\n| „Spirou and Fantasio“ | Spirou and Fantasio | Marsupilami |"]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",800],["+","Die belgische Zeitschrift „Spirou“ brachte einen Sidekick hervor, der wilder ist als jeder Hund. Am 31. Januar 1952 ließ André Franquin Spirou und Fantasio ein Marsupilami nach Hause bringen, ein wehrhaftes, schwarz-gelbes Tier aus dem südamerikanischen Dschungel von Palumbien, gefleckt wie ein Leopard und mit einem absurd langen Greifschwanz, den es als Faust, Sprungfeder und Lasso benutzt. Es sagt selten mehr als „Houba! Houba!“, wuchs aber bald über die Serie hinaus und bekam eigene Alben, Zeichentrickserien und Filme.\n\n"],["=",87],["+","\n| „Spirou und Fantasio“ | Spirou und Fantasio | Marsupilami |"]]}]},
